` Evil Sift Workbench — documented SPL searches `
` ============================================== `
` These are the searches an analyst would run in their own Splunk
` environment to produce the exports that splunk_export_adapter.py consumes.
` Nothing in this repo connects to a live Splunk instance: run a search,
` export the results as JSON (Web UI "Export > Format: JSON", or the REST
` API with output_mode=json), then feed the file to the adapter:
`
`   python3 splunk_export_adapter.py <export.json> --out out/splunk/events.jsonl
`
` The fake files next to this one (incident_search_results.json,
` benign_export_stream.jsonl, injection_flat_export.jsonl) are hand-written
` stand-ins for what these searches would return. All data is fake.

` --- Search 1: Windows authentication events (CIM Authentication) ---------
` Splunk Add-on for Windows v5+: channel lives in source, sourcetype is WinEventLog.
index=wineventlog sourcetype=WinEventLog source=WinEventLog:Security (EventCode=4625 OR EventCode=4624)
| fields _time host source sourcetype index EventCode action app user src dest Logon_Type signature _raw

` --- Search 2: Endpoint process + network telemetry (Sysmon) --------------
` Splunk Add-on for Sysmon: sourcetype XmlWinEventLog, channel in source.
index=sysmon sourcetype=XmlWinEventLog source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" (EventCode=1 OR EventCode=3)
| fields _time host source sourcetype index EventCode user process process_name parent_process_name src dest_ip dest_port transport dest signature _raw

` --- Search 3: Zeek conn logs with asset enrichment -----------------------
` TA for Zeek ingests conn logs as bro:conn:json. The lookup attributes
` sensor-collected flows back to the monitored asset, so chain detection can
` correlate execution and egress on the same host.
index=zeek sourcetype=bro:conn:json
| lookup assets_by_ip ip AS src_ip OUTPUTNEW asset AS orig_host
| fields _time host orig_host source sourcetype index src_ip dest_ip dest_port id.orig_h id.resp_h id.resp_p proto service conn_state orig_bytes resp_bytes _raw

` --- Round trip: view Evil Sift findings back in Splunk -------------------
` After POSTing out/splunk/*/hec_events.jsonl to your HTTP Event Collector
` (see scripts/findings_to_hec.py for the documented curl command):
sourcetype=evil_sift:finding
| table _time host severity confidence score tactic title evidence_ids input_sha256
| sort - score
